From 83f01b5048b75f1a1beb6aaf99da50348a6dfe70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: memra-lane <lane@localhost>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 07:30:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] dsv4 dense: a gate-only arm for the tensor-core path, so
 a class cell can take both arms in one process

NOT a door. No environment read, no serving caller, no dispatch a serving
process can reach: when the CUTLASS archive is linked this path is the code.
The switch exists because a CLASS comparison has to take both arms over ONE
tape in ONE process. Two binaries cannot share a model load, and a drift row
measured across two loads carries the load's variation into the number it is
trying to attribute to a reduction tree. memra #482 set the precedent with
arm_reference_expert_program_for_gate().

Standing the path down returns 40080 BEFORE admission, so it is not counted or
announced as a decline: no shape was rejected.

The wrappers in dsv4_gpu.cu are linked unconditionally and return 40084 when
the archive is absent, so arm_dense_cutlass_for_gate() gives a named refusal
instead of a link error, and dense_cutlass_armed_for_gate() returns None rather
than false. A class cell whose two arms are secretly the same program has to
fail, not report zero drift: that is the mistake this lane already made once,
when a served A/B compared two byte-identical binaries.

Signed-off-by: memra-lane <lane@localhost>
