From 54c46bf117b6c30829827c7eeda8dbbb6c141e4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: memra-lane <lane@localhost>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:10:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] dsv4 dense: both arms, one model load, no server, so the
 next question can be asked at all

The served 37% is not the kernel and not the family: the per-shape setup cache
retired the host hypothesis (0.027 us per call) and the family bench runs both
real kernels over the real census counts at three weight-residency levels with
the CUTLASS arm winning every one (5.93x in L2, 4.55x with 3.15 GB of codes and
6.31 GB of mirror cycling past it). That leaves the engine's surroundings, and
narrowing them needs a cell with no HTTP, no sampler, no spec route and no
second process: one load, the same prompt, the arm flipped between timed
prefills, at the served width of 512 rather than the 64 every earlier receipt
in this lane used.

The three non-vacuity checks are the ones this lane learned the hard way: the
path must be PRESENT (absent and off are different facts and look identical in
a timing row), the ON arm must run split-K calls, and the OFF arm must run
none.

Signed-off-by: memra-lane <lane@localhost>
---
